{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfTi5VYqAbFS9bQ8b8iV7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HVdrzVdojLqJ73EQ4S9BQ1","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/jcarr/.cache/markdownattractor/bench/t4/qmd/src/apps/docs/content/docs/orm/v7/prisma-client/deployment/traditional/deploy-to-koyeb.mdx","offset":169,"limit":30},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":270,"cache_read_input_tokens":20946,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":270},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dbe9641c-40c4-48ff-bfc4-1b2d0a4c61d0","uuid":"6416bae3-a63b-4155-88d7-c7cd46c10b0f","timestamp":"2026-09-27T09:29:33.767Z","request_id":"req_011CfTi5Uv8ion76bL85hGLh","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01HVdrzVdojLqJ73EQ4S9BQ1":{"file_path":"/Users/jcarr/.cache/markdownattractor/bench/t4/qmd/src/apps/docs/content/docs/orm/v7/prisma-client/deployment/traditional/deploy-to-koyeb.mdx","offset":169,"limit":30}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HVdrzVdojLqJ73EQ4S9BQ1","type":"tool_result","content":"169\t## Koyeb specific notes\n170\t\n171\t### Build\n172\t\n173\tBy default, for applications using the Node.js runtime, if the `package.json` contains a `build` script, Koyeb automatically executes it after the dependencies installation.\n174\tIn the example, the `build` script is used to run `prisma generate && prisma migrate deploy && next build`.\n175\t\n176\t### Deployment\n177\t\n178\tBy default, for applications using the Node.js runtime, if the `package.json` contains a `start` script, Koyeb automatically executes it to launch the application.\n179\tIn the example, the `start` script is used to run `node src/index.js`.\n180\t\n181\t### Database migrations and deployments\n182\t\n183\tIn the example you deployed, migrations are applied using the `prisma migrate deploy` command during the Koyeb build (as defined in the `build` script in `package.json`).\n184\t\n185\t### Additional notes\n186\t\n187\tIn this guide, we kept pre-set values for the region, instance size, and horizontal scaling. You can customize them according to your needs.\n188\t\n189\t> **Note:** The Ports section is used to let Koyeb know which port your application is listening to and properly route incoming HTTP requests. A default `PORT` environment variable is set to `8080` and incoming HTTP requests are routed to the `/` path when creating a new application.\n190\t> If your application is listening on another port, you can define another port to route incoming HTTP requests.\n191\t\n192\t## Summary\n193\t\n194\tCongratulations! You have successfully deployed a Node.js app with Prisma ORM to Koyeb.\n195\t\n196\tYou can find the source code for the example in [this GitHub repository](https://github.com/koyeb/example-prisma).\n197\t\n198\tFor more insight into Prisma Client's API, look at the route handlers in the `src/index.js` file."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dbe9641c-40c4-48ff-bfc4-1b2d0a4c61d0","uuid":"d3357406-d6f3-4efa-b15e-986382a0fb82","timestamp":"2026-09-27T09:29:33.787Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/jcarr/.cache/markdownattractor/bench/t4/qmd/src/apps/docs/content/docs/orm/v7/prisma-client/deployment/traditional/deploy-to-koyeb.mdx","content":"## Koyeb specific notes\n\n### Build\n\nBy default, for applications using the Node.js runtime, if the `package.json` contains a `build` script, Koyeb automatically executes it after the dependencies installation.\nIn the example, the `build` script is used to run `prisma generate && prisma migrate deploy && next build`.\n\n### Deployment\n\nBy default, for applications using the Node.js runtime, if the `package.json` contains a `start` script, Koyeb automatically executes it to launch the application.\nIn the example, the `start` script is used to run `node src/index.js`.\n\n### Database migrations and deployments\n\nIn the example you deployed, migrations are applied using the `prisma migrate deploy` command during the Koyeb build (as defined in the `build` script in `package.json`).\n\n### Additional notes\n\nIn this guide, we kept pre-set values for the region, instance size, and horizontal scaling. You can customize them according to your needs.\n\n> **Note:** The Ports section is used to let Koyeb know which port your application is listening to and properly route incoming HTTP requests. A default `PORT` environment variable is set to `8080` and incoming HTTP requests are routed to the `/` path when creating a new application.\n> If your application is listening on another port, you can define another port to route incoming HTTP requests.\n\n## Summary\n\nCongratulations! You have successfully deployed a Node.js app with Prisma ORM to Koyeb.\n\nYou can find the source code for the example in [this GitHub repository](https://github.com/koyeb/example-prisma).\n\nFor more insight into Prisma Client's API, look at the route handlers in the `src/index.js` file.","numLines":30,"startLine":169,"totalLines":199}}}
